TEXT -96 -200 Left 3 ;#55 Parallel LC circuit below, at and above resonance
TEXT -96 -144 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hqhV50852jA
TEXT -96 -104 Left 2 ;The generator drives L1 and C1 in parallel at 20 kHz, at the 33.9 kHz resonance, and at 50 kHz (one stepped run).
TEXT -96 -72 Left 2 ;At resonance the L1 and C1 currents cancel, the tank draws almost nothing, and CH1 rises to the open-circuit generator voltage.
TEXT 640 16 Left 2 ;CH1: voltage across the L1 || C1 tank (Alan's channel 1).  V1: 4 V p-p open circuit, Rser = 50 ohm generator output.
TEXT 640 48 Left 2 ;Assumed (not stated in the video): L1 = 220 uH with 1 ohm winding resistance, C1 = 100 nF, so f0 = 33.9 kHz.
TEXT 640 128 Left 2 !.tran 0 300u 200u 50n
TEXT 640 168 Left 2 !.step param f list 20k 33.93k 50k
TEXT 640 208 Left 2 !.meas tran TANK_PP PP V(ch1) FROM 200u TO 300u
TEXT 640 248 Left 2 !.meas tran IL_PP PP I(L1) FROM 200u TO 300u
TEXT 640 288 Left 2 !.meas tran IGEN_PP PP I(V1) FROM 200u TO 300u
